1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,930
Job hunting is the same work, over and over. DevJobInfo takes that part off your hands.

2
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:11,900
Everything lands on one dashboard — jobs found, your match rate, and where every application stands.

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,510
Plus how your match scores are spread, and your weekly AI spend, so you always know where things stand.

4
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:22,780
It all rests on your profile. Drop in your CV, and it fills itself in.

5
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:28,640
Search five job boards at once — or paste a job URL straight in.

6
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:38,340
Every job is scored against your profile. And a thin posting gets capped, never oversold — so you know exactly which ones are worth your time.

7
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:45,650
Behind the scenes, DevJobInfo researches the company — and pulls its actual colors and fonts into your materials, so everything looks like it belongs there.

8
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:53,560
Then a cover letter, written from your real history, in the language of the posting — drawing on your own saved snippets and past letters.

9
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:58,060
A short, AI-written headline tops it off — one click to regenerate it on its own.

10
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,450
Nothing invented — only what's actually in your profile.

11
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:07,570
And because it's AI-written, we run it through an AI-detector — then rewrite anything that sounds too robotic, until it sounds like you again.

12
00:01:08,570 --> 00:01:22,140
Before you send anything, we simulate how an Applicant Tracking System actually reads it — resume and cover letter both — so nothing gets lost to a bot before a person ever sees it. Regenerate the letter and it automatically fixes what the review flagged.

13
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:29,800
Add your own motivation for the role, so it never reads like it was written by a bot.

14
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:40,190
And a resume tailored to this job, reordered around what this employer asked for — including a version built specifically to pass ATS parsing.

15
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:45,030
Both download as polished PDFs, ready to send the moment you find the job.

16
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:52,770
Every AI feature runs on your own key — Claude, Mistral, OpenAI, Grok, or Gemini, whichever you choose — so there's no subscription, and you're never locked to one provider.

17
00:01:53,770 --> 00:01:55,280
DevJobInfo — devjob dot info.

